%U A397436 2849038731540183108,100404579055634969212,3556236503353046684948,126511489816953333410380,4517959963709386024502320,161896622686217806310433400,5819113079819855757874995216
%N A397436 a(n) = Sum_{k = 0..n} binomial(n+k-1, k)*binomial(3*n+k-1, k).
%C A397436 Conjectures:
%C A397436 1) The supercongruence a(p^r) == a(p^(r-1)) (mod p^(3*r+3)) holds for all primes p >= 5 and integers r >= 2.
%C A397436 2) The supercongruence a(n*p^r) == a(n*p^(r-1)) (mod p^(3*r)) holds for all primes p >= 5 and integers n >= 2, r >= 1.
%C A397436 3) More generally, let m_1, ..., m_r be integers and M a positive integer. Define u(n) = Sum_{k = 0..M*n} binomial(m_1*n, k)*...* binomial(m_r*n, k). The supercongruence u(p^r) == u(p^(r-1)) (mod p^(3*r)) holds for all primes p >= 5 and all positive integers r (the present sequence is the case M = 1, m_1 = -1 and m_2 = -3).
%C A397436 Sum_{k = 0..n} binomial(n, k)*binomial(3*n, k) = binomial(4*n,n). - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Aug 07 2026
%F A397436 a(n) = Sum_{k = 0..n} binomial(-n, k)*binomial(-3*n, k).
%F A397436 The supercongruence a(p) == a(1) (mod p^5) holds for all primes p >= 7.
%F A397436 From _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Aug 07 2026: (Start)
%F A397436 Recurrence: 24*n^2*(2*n - 1)*(3*n - 2)*(3*n - 1)*(4*n - 3)*(4*n - 1)*(37345*n^7 - 389126*n^6 + 1733014*n^5 - 4276384*n^4 + 6314577*n^3 - 5579730*n^2 + 2731936*n - 571776)*a(n) = (9816992185*n^1^4 - 136636579393*n^1^3 + 862919087447*n^1^2 - 3272194759213*n^1^1 + 8308992204417*n^1^0 - 14918925747783*n^9 + 19496981342093*n^8 - 18805075026551*n^7 + 13427650735450*n^6 - 7051911236180*n^5 + 2677493942664*n^4 - 711899298432*n^3 + 125230551552*n^2 - 13052067840*n + 609638400)*a(n-1) - 48*(n-2)*(2*n - 3)^2*(3*n - 5)*(3*n - 4)*(4*n - 7)*(4*n - 5)*(37345*n^7 - 127711*n^6 + 182503*n^5 - 141129*n^4 + 63736*n^3 - 16808*n^2 + 2400*n - 144)*a(n-2).
%F A397436 a(n) ~ 2^(10*n + 1/2) / (7*Pi*n * 3^(3*n - 1/2)). (End)
%e A397436 Example of supercongruences:
%e A397436 a(19) - a(1) = 5819113079819855757874995216 - 4 = (2^2)*(19^5)*47*119971*
%e A397436 104196867730981 == 0 (mod 19^5).
%p A397436 seq(add(binomial(n+k-1, k)*binomial(3*n+k-1, k), k = 0..n), n = 0..20);
%t A397436 Table[Sum[Binomial[-n, k]*Binomial[-3*n, k], {k, 0, n}], {n, 0, 20}] (* _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Aug 07 2026 *)
